@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Experimental older-CPU ISA emulation (Q8400 research)
+
+This is an experimental, fail-closed extension of the v0.4 ISA rewrite. It is **not a complete AVX emulator** and does not claim that CTR Nitro-Fueled will run on a Core 2 Quad Q8400.
+
+## What it adds
+
+- `POPCNT` software emulation, including the architecturally defined flags.
+- `CRC32` (SSE4.2 CRC32C) and `PCMPGTQ` emulation.
+- A software shadow for the upper 128 bits of each YMM register, per thread. Low XMM halves are saved/restored by rewrite stubs and copied through the OS trap context for INT3 sites. MXCSR is propagated through the trap context.
+- AVX emulation for `VZEROUPPER`, `VZEROALL`, unaligned `VMOVUPS`, `VMOVUPD`, `VMOVDQU`, `VMOVMSKPS/PD`, `VPMOVMSKB`, packed bitwise operations (`VAND*`, `VANDN*`, `VOR*`, `VXOR*`), packed/scalar add/subtract/multiply/divide, `VSHUFPS/PD`, `VPSHUFD`, `VPERM2F128/I128`, `VINSERTF128`, `VEXTRACTF128` and immediate blend operations in the scanner allowlist.
+- The scanner now records other VEX instructions as unsupported and prints their mnemonic counts. The loader refuses to rewrite/run when the current CPU is missing AVX/SSE4.2 and any required site is unsupported. This is deliberate; it avoids an illegal instruction crash after a partial rewrite.
+
+## Not yet implemented
+
+Many AVX/AVX2 instructions are not emulated: other shuffle/permutation/blend forms, compares, conversions, gathers, most integer AVX2 operations and several other families. Aligned vector moves are also intentionally excluded because they must reproduce alignment-fault behavior. SSE4.2 string-comparison instructions (`PCMPESTRI/M`, `PCMPISTRI/M`) are reported unsupported. F16C remains unsupported. If any of these instructions occur in the prepared executable, the runtime will stop and list the count rather than pretending compatibility.
+
+## Tests
+
+The standalone C tests exercise the emulated vector operations, YMM upper-half shadow, CRC32C, POPCNT and rewrite-stub size. Build them on an x86-64 GCC/Clang host with:
+
+```sh
+cc -std=c11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -mno-avx -mno-avx2 -mno-sse4.2 -mno-popcnt -mno-bmi -mno-lzcnt -mno-movbe -mno-f16c -Isrc src/isa_emulate.c tests/test_isa_emulate.c -o /tmp/isa-emulate-test
+/tmp/isa-emulate-test
+cc -std=c11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -mno-avx -mno-avx2 -mno-sse4.2 -mno-popcnt -mno-bmi -mno-lzcnt -mno-movbe -mno-f16c -Isrc src/isa_emulate.c src/isa_rewrite.c tests/test_isa_rewrite_stub.c -o /tmp/isa-rewrite-test
+/tmp/isa-rewrite-test
+```
+
+The C smoke tests passed in the development environment. The full Windows build and scanner against the user's prepared `boot-linked.bin` have not been run here; the Linux environment does not have the `iced_x86` native decoder installed. Do not use `BB_SKIP_CPU_CHECK=1` as a substitute for instruction emulation.
